From c13e11eb26ec949efafa38ed5ddb202e7853352d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 02:17:49 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] feat(app,ui): fixture plates - a parametric grid/dowel
 plate, fixtures placed at grid holes
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A built-in, parametric fixture (tooling) plate in the fixture library,
following the built-in vise pattern: a generated solid-slab mesh placed
through InsertFixture, its grid riding FixtureDef (plate::PlateLink).

- Plate: length/width/thickness, hole grid (pitch X/Y, first-hole
  offset), thread, optional dowel lattice and counterbores; refused by
  name when nonsensical. Presets: 12 x 12 in, 300 x 300 mm, 400 x 300 mm
  and one sized from the 770MX machine file's table; "on the table"
  centres a plate on the setup machine's table.
- Grid names: rows lettered along +Y from A, columns numbered along +X
  from 1, A1 nearest the plate frame's origin corner.
- PlaceOnPlate: any fixture at a grid hole or on a dowel pair, standing
  on the plate top, turned by a yaw; the place is recorded, MoveFixture
  carries a plate's fixtures (transitively) in its one undo step, and
  SetPlate re-seats them on the new grid. Unknown locations, gaps,
  overhangs, cycles and bad turns are refused by name.
- SetPlateGrid: an imported plate's grid from its detected holes (the
  Detect holes rule), regular or staggered, with gaps named.
- Project file: optional `plate` / `on_plate` keys read leniently
  (dropped and logged, never a failed load); no version bump.
- MCP: add_fixture_plate, set_fixture_plate, place_on_plate,
  detect_plate_grid, get_plate_grid.
- UI: "Add fixture plate…" dialog, plate rows, the grid-location
  picker, "Detect plate grid", and viewport hole markers.

Fixes #819

